1
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:10,020
A photo is 10 centimetres by 15 centimetres.

2
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:14,500
It is enlarged by scale factor 3 to make a poster.

3
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:18,860
How does the area change: 9 times bigger, or 3 times bigger?

4
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:22,220
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:23,390
9 times bigger.

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:29,380
Both the length and the width are multiplied by 3, and 3 times 3 is 9.

7
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:34,620
Remember: in an enlargement, every length is multiplied by the scale factor.

8
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:36,900
The angles stay the same.

9
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:44,770
When lengths are multiplied by K, the perimeter is multiplied by K, but the area is multiplied by K squared.

10
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:45,440
Your turn.

11
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:49,070
What is the area of the poster, in square centimetres?

12
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:52,290
Pause the video and try it.

13
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:55,130
30 times 45 is 1,350.

14
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:58,930
Or 150 times 9 is 1,350.

15
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:03,460
The scale factor is the image length divided by the object length.

16
00:01:03,510 --> 00:01:08,480
To find the centre, draw lines through matching corners, and extend them.

17
00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:10,680
They meet at the centre.

18
00:01:10,730 --> 00:01:12,050
Here is the method.

19
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,760
Step 1: find the scale factor.

20
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:19,070
Step 2: from the centre, multiply each distance by K.

21
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:23,900
Step 3: lengths and perimeter times K; area times K squared.

22
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:27,240
Step 4: check the angles are the same.

23
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:31,870
Enlarge the point 5, 3 by scale factor 2, with centre 1, 1.

24
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,630
From the centre, the point is 4 across and 2 up.

25
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,910
Double it: 8 across and 4 up.

26
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,870
The image is 9, 5.

27
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:40,640
Your turn.

28
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:45,190
Enlarge the point 4, 2 by scale factor 3, with centre 1, 1.

29
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:48,290
Pause and work it out.

30
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:51,220
From the centre: 3 across and 1 up.

31
00:01:51,270 --> 00:01:53,480
Times 3: 9 across and 3 up.

32
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,620
The image is 10, 4.

33
00:01:55,670 --> 00:02:00,060
A 4 by 6 rectangle is enlarged by scale factor 2.5.

34
00:02:00,110 --> 00:02:05,660
The area 24 is multiplied by 6.25: 150 square centimetres.

35
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:09,280
A 3 by 5 rectangle is enlarged by scale factor 2.

36
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,980
Zoe finds the new area.

37
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:13,010
Which line is wrong?

38
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,180
Line 1 is wrong.

39
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:18,540
Both lengths double, so the area is multiplied by 4.

40
00:02:18,590 --> 00:02:22,590
6 times 10 is 60 square centimetres.

41
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:28,750
Doubling the width and height of a printed photo uses about four times as much ink.

42
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,150
One last question.

43
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,570
Two similar shapes have areas of 12 and 108.

44
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:35,520
What is the scale factor?

45
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:39,020
Pause the video and answer.

46
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:41,100
108 divided by 12 is 9.

47
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:44,270
That is K squared, so K is 3.

48
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:48,670
To remember: lengths and perimeter are multiplied by K.

49
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:51,480
Area is multiplied by K squared.

50
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:55,520
K is the image length divided by the object length.

51
00:02:55,570 --> 00:02:58,140
Ray lines meet at the centre.

52
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:03,590
Great work! Now practise lesson 13.4 on Camday.
